From aa9f00317aed874c8734511fbb45788763ac8fac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 21:45:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] vrend: do not require EXT_texture_shadow_lod for a
 gather

For TGSI_OPCODE_TG4 the operand slot the emitter calls the bias holds
the shadow comparison value, so every textureGather on a 2D-array or
cube shadow sampler asked the host for EXT_texture_shadow_lod. A gather
on a shadow sampler is core GLSL and a desktop GL host has no reason to
implement that extension, so the generated shader failed to compile and
put the context into error, which on this host costs the rest of the
run rather than the one draw.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vrend/vrend_shader.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c b/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
index 39895ce..3bad057 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
@@ -3366,8 +3366,12 @@ static void translate_tex(struct dump_ctx *ctx,
 
    bool has_bias = strbuf_get_len (&bias_buf) != 0;
    bool has_offset = strbuf_get_len (&offset_buf) != 0;
-   // EXT_texture_shadow_lod defines a few more functions handling bias
-   if (has_bias &&
+   // EXT_texture_shadow_lod defines a few more functions handling bias.
+   // TG4 is not one of them: for a gather the same slot carries the shadow
+   // comparison value, and textureGather on a shadow sampler is core GLSL.
+   // Requiring the extension there fails to compile on a host that has no
+   // reason to implement it.
+   if (has_bias && inst->Instruction.Opcode != TGSI_OPCODE_TG4 &&
        (inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOW2D_ARRAY ||
         inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOWCUBE ||
         inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOWCUBE_ARRAY))
